<Base title="Videos" description="Seminar presentations, lectures, and workshops on depth psychology, addiction recovery, and the archetype of the Alcoholic by Cody Peterson." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article>
    <h1>Videos</h1>
    <p>Seminars, lectures, and workshops on depth psychology, the archetype of the Alcoholic, and Jungian approaches to recovery.</p>

    <h2>Dreamwork: Dreams and Symbols of Recovery</h2>
    <p>A four-part series presented for Friendly Circle Berlin, April 2025.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EzDFZsEOMVQ" target="_blank">Dreamwork 1: Alchemical Symbolism and Modern Dreams</a></h3>
    <p>Cody introduces dream interpretation from the lens of Carl Jung's contributions to alchemy. Examines different ways to interpret dreams, with audience Q&amp;A.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TvrcDw0CB8I" target="_blank">Dreamwork 2: The Divine Feminine</a></h3>
    <p>Cody dives deeper into the anima, examining the Gnostic figure of Sophia, the divine feminine trapped in matter, and her relationship to the modern masculine psyche.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tqZl1kvvZSM" target="_blank">Dreamwork 3: Mercurius</a></h3>
    <p>Cody introduces the alchemical concept of Mercurius, a duplex character equated with the Trickster and the Alcoholic, and examines the relationship between Mercurius and the anima.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P9D_28CEAqs" target="_blank">Dreamwork 4: The Philosopher's Stone</a></h3>
    <p>Cody takes us through the alchemical concept of the philosopher's stone, squaring the circle, the four functions, and mythological context for the coniunctio.</p>

    <h2>The Archetype of the Alcoholic Seminars</h2>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E_BuFNpGE_A" target="_blank">The Mystery of the Coniunctio: Unpacking Jung's Helpful Formula</a></h3>
    <p>A deep dive into the psychology behind Jung's statement Spiritus Contra Spiritum, exploring the coniunctio oppositorum through the lens of the archetype of the Alcoholic.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GxhOhJ056WQ" target="_blank">The Archetype of the Alcoholic (Part One)</a></h3>
    <p>Cody introduces his conception of the Archetype of the Alcoholic, comparing it to the ancient energy known as the Trickster/Shaman.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2S3wafhxo0Y" target="_blank">Chapter Seventeen: Doorways to the Self</a></h3>
    <p>A chapter-by-chapter discussion exploring how the Twelve Steps function as doorways to what Jung called the Self.</p>

    <h2>Emotional Sobriety</h2>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sDYXCBCN3KQ" target="_blank">Introduction: A Case for Coming Down</a></h3>
    <p>Cody introduces the concept of emotional sobriety and makes the case for descent — why recovery requires more than spiritual ascent.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kDZG3sBqap4" target="_blank">Monotheism, Misogyny, and Eusebia</a></h3>
    <p>How Western culture's monotheistic bias has shaped recovery programs. Drawing on Corbin, Hillman, and Welwood, Cody traces how serenity became an idol and turns to the Greek notion of eusebia.</p>

    <h2>Friendly Circle Berlin Workshops</h2>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h1gzmto1ZLQ" target="_blank">C.G. Jung &amp; Recovery: From Trickster to Shaman (Part 1)</a></h3>
    <p>The first of a collaborative workshop series exploring the intersection of Jungian thought and the history of recovery.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jBZ9FhyrgNY" target="_blank">The Birth of AA: Jung to Bill W. (Part 2)</a></h3>
    <p>Tracing the historical and psychological lineage from Jung's encounter with Rowland Hazard to the founding of Alcoholics Anonymous.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g5lVdXRL-Yc" target="_blank">The Transformative Power of Storytelling in Recovery (with Bill Schaberg)</a></h3>
    <p>A conversation with Bill Schaberg on the role of narrative and storytelling in the recovery process.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ifWIU05f7UY" target="_blank">Carl Jung, Bill Wilson &amp; AA's Spiritual Roots</a></h3>
    <p>Introduction by Cody Peterson for Ian McCabe's presentation on the spiritual foundations of AA.</p>

    <h3><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hEXrBZ3qxOk" target="_blank">Big Book History #23: Storytelling in Recovery (with Bill Schaberg)</a></h3>
    <p>An interview with Bill Schaberg exploring the narrative traditions embedded in the Big Book.</p>

    <p style="margin-top: 2.5rem; color: var(--color-text-muted);">
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@cody-peterson-author" target="_blank">Watch all videos on YouTube →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
